@startuml
title Calli: native writer and trust boundaries
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Calli service (local or Windows demo VM)" {
  [Microphone] as Mic
  [New Pronote dictation\ncontext checks, correct, STOP] as UI
  [Local structurer\nutterance -> student + text] as Struct
  database "Guarded item queue\n+ STOP file" as Queue
  [Verifier\ncompare reported identity\nand read-back to queued item] as Verifier
  database "Journal (JSONL)\nbefore, after, status" as Journal
  [Scoreboard\nREADME table] as Report
  [Custom tools\nnext_item, report_result] as Tools
}

package "Gladia" {
  [Live speech-to-text\ncustom vocabulary = roster] as STT
}

package "H Company" {
  [Computer-use agent\nHolo model] as Agent
  [Environment\ncloud browser | Windows desktop] as Env
}

package "Target software (no API, untrusted content)" {
  [Moodle demo\nassignment feedback] as Moodle
  [PRONOTE client\nBulletins > Appréciations] as Pronote
}

Mic --> STT
STT --> Struct
Struct --> UI
UI --> Queue : guarded completed dictation\nor confirmed correction
Queue --> Tools
Tools <--> Agent : next_item / report_result
Agent --> Env
Env --> Moodle
Env --> Pronote
Tools --> Verifier
Verifier --> Journal
Verifier --> Queue : optional corrective retry\n(disabled in presentation run)
Journal --> Report
UI ..> Queue : STOP drains the queue

note right of Verifier
  The status of an item is decided here,
  by checking the reported identity and text.
  This is not an independent visual audit.
end note

note bottom of Pronote
  Text visible on the screen is data for the agent,
  never an instruction (write policy, injection fixture).
end note
@enduml
